{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stampable-sunbeamy-jackal","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nEvery CI job makes an avoidable network call to `raw.githubusercontent.com` before it can start, and when that call fails the job fails with `##[error]fetch failed` — a failure with no relationship to the change under test.\n\nObserved 2026-08-28 on the `pip-audit` job of run 33214025855, which died after 21 seconds. The three consecutive log lines name the whole causal chain:\n\n```\nCould not determine uv version from uv.toml or pyproject.toml. Falling back ...\nFetching manifest data from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh ...\n##[error]fetch failed\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `astral-sh/setup-uv` action is correctly SHA-pinned at every call site (`ae62891fec2bb8e7d6c99fc78c9fec3a63790f8d  # v10.0.0`) — but **uv itself is not pinned**. There is no `version:` input at any call site, no `[tool.uv] required-version` in `pyproject.toml`, and no `uv.toml`. With no locally-determinable version the action falls back to resolving one from a remote manifest, so a network dependency is introduced on every run of every workflow that installs uv.\n\nAffected call sites (at least 8): `_build-and-test.yml:63`, `:264`, `_mutation.yml:56`, `:121`, `_eval-discipline.yml:59`, `dependency-advisory-canary.yml:85`, `release.yml:107`.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than rechecking\n\nThis is the class of failure that gets labelled \"environmental\" and retried, and each retry costs a full CI run and — on a Gerrit change — resets the votes. It is not genuinely environmental: the network call exists only because we did not pin a version, so the fix removes the failure mode instead of tolerating it.\n\nIt also contradicts practice this project already applies elsewhere: `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` pins `acli` by version AND sha256 with the explicit instruction \"Never run `latest` in CI.\"\n\n`release.yml` is on the list, so an unpinned uv is also a supply-chain surface on the publishing path: the resolved version can change between runs without any change to the repository.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] uv is pinned to an explicit version reachable without a network manifest fetch, at every `setup-uv` call site (or once, in a project file the action reads).\n- [ ] A CI run produces no `Could not determine uv version` line and no manifest fetch from `raw.githubusercontent.com`.\n- [ ] The pin is single-sourced rather than duplicated across 8 call sites, or — if per-site inputs are required — a check fails when the sites disagree.\n- [ ] Upgrading uv remains a deliberate, reviewable one-line change.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Assert on a real CI log: the `Could not determine uv version` line must be ABSENT after the change. **Anchor it** — first assert a line that proves the setup step actually ran (so an empty log or a skipped step cannot pass the check), then assert the fallback line is gone. A grep returning zero matches proves nothing on its own.\n- If the pin is single-sourced, add a check that every call site resolves to that source, and prove the check FAILS when one site is deliberately skewed.\n- Confirm the installed uv version in a run matches the pin, rather than only confirming the fallback message disappeared.","id":"56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CI depends on an avoidable network fetch on every job: uv is unpinned, so setup-uv falls back to fetching a remote manifest"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787970419925883001,"uuid":"9962e136-4568-4a71-bbd5-5dffdd8132b5"}